<!-- Template Description -->
This template creates a tabbed interface.
It supports deep-linking to specific tabs if a unique ID is provided.

==Hiding a tab==
<code>hide''N''</code> removes a tab completely — useful for parking a section that isn't ready without deleting its content.

<pre>{{Tabber|tab1=Shown|content1=Visible|tab2=Parked|content2=Not ready|hide2=true}}</pre>

The value must be exactly <code>true</code> (case-insensitive). <code>yes</code> or <code>1</code> will '''not''' hide the tab.

Tabs must also be numbered '''consecutively''' — the first missing <code>tab''N''</code> stops the sequence, so hiding a middle tab with <code>hide2=true</code> is correct, but deleting <code>tab2</code> outright would discard tab 3 onward.

==Syntax==
{{T|Tabber
|v1=id=tabber id
|v2=tabN=Nth Tab Name
|v3=contentN=Content for Nth tab
|v4=hideN=true
|block=1
}}

Replace '''N''' with consecutive numbers starting at <code>1</code> — <code>tab1</code>/<code>content1</code>, <code>tab2</code>/<code>content2</code>, and so on. The template stops at the first missing <code>tab''N''</code>, so gaps in the numbering discard every tab after the gap.

==Examples==
=== Basic Usage ===
{{T|Tabber
|p1=tab1=First Tab
|p2=content1=Content for first tab
|p3=tab2=Second Tab
|p4=content2=Content for second tab
|block=1
|_Y_=1
}}

=== Usage with a Unique ID (for deep-linking) ===
To allow linking directly to a specific tab, and to prevent conflicts when using multiple tabbers on the same page, provide a unique '''id''' for the tabber group.

{{T|Tabber
|p1=id=unique-page-id-for-this-tabber
|p2=tab1=Overview
|p3=content1=This section contains text with {{!}} pipes {{!}} and [[links]]
|p4=tab2=Details
|p5=content2={{Template:TrackTable|param1|param2}} 
|block=1
|_Y_=1
}}
This will generate URL hashes like '''#unique-page-id-for-this-tabber-Overview''' when a tab is clicked.


